WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
EPA 608 is not optional. You cannot legally touch refrigerant without it. Let's
make sure you pass.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:20.000
ASHRAE Standard 15 is the Safety Standard for Refrigeration Systems. It governs
equipment room requirements, refrigerant detector placement, ventilation rates,
and emergency shutoffs. ASHRAE Standard 34 assigns safety group designations to

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:40.000
ASHRAE 15: Safety Standard for Refrigeration Systems. Covers equipment rooms,
ventilation, and emergency shutoffs.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:50.000
ASHRAE 34: Refrigerant designation and safety classification standard. Assigns
A/B toxicity and 1/2L/2/3 flammability ratings.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:01:00.000
A2L: Low toxicity, mildly flammable. Burning velocity 10 cm/s or less. Includes
R-32, R-454B, R-466A.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Here's why this matters on the job: When you see a new refrigerant on a system
nameplate, the ASHRAE 34 safety group tells you immediately what precautions to
take before you open anything.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:20.000
Watch out for these: A2L refrigerants require A2L-rated equipment — you cannot
retrofit. And B-class refrigerants like R-123 require more ventilation and PPE.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Quick check: what is the maximum fine for knowingly venting refrigerant? If you
don't know that number, go back and read it again.

